hw/sh4: ze0 2D engine display-list interpreter (TODO M8.C1f).

After ze0-0013 the UI submits 2DG display lists (DLSAR + SCLR = 1) but
nothing executed them, so no frame reached the screen planes.  The new
hw/sh4/ze0_2dg.c runs a list synchronously when SCLR = 1 is written,
before SR.TRA is raised.  The command set is reconstructed from the
lists the firmware builds (auirtdll.dll) and covers what the map and
the boot screens use: calls/returns, register writes (direct and from
inline data), inline data blocks, sync, end, filled boxes, 8-bit alpha
glyphs, stencil polygons with cover fill, polylines (inline vertices or
by pointer) and textured quads (nearest sampling).  Pixels are
(A)RGB1555.  Unknown commands are skipped up to the next command word
and counted.

New ze0-gfx property exec (default on); with gfx-trace=on each list
logs "ze0-2dg: list ADDR: N drawn, M skipped, S steps".


